{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++14 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++14 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nusing ll = long long;\nconstexpr int MOD = 1000000007;\nconstexpr int MAXN = 32;\n\nint n;\n\nstruct Matrix {\n    int a[MAXN][MAXN];\n    Matrix() { memset(a, 0, sizeof(a)); }\n    void clear() { memset(a, 0, sizeof(a)); }\n    void output() {\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n + 1; ++i) {\n            for (int j = 1; j <= n + 1; ++j) {\n                printf(\"%d%c\", a[i][j], j == n + 1 ? '\\n' : ' ');\n            }\n        }\n        putchar('\\n');\n    }\n    Matrix operator*(const Matrix& rhs) const {\n        Matrix res;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n + 1; ++i) {\n            for (int j = 1; j <= n + 1; ++j) {\n                for (int k = 1; k <= n + 1; ++k) {\n                    res.a[i][j] = (res.a[i][j] + 1LL * a[i][k] * rhs.a[k][j]) % MOD;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n};\n\nMatrix ans, E, A[MAXN], pre[MAXN], suf[MAXN];\n\nint readInt() {\n    int x = 0, f = 1;\n    char c = getchar();\n    while (c < '0' || c > '9') { if (c == '-') f = -1; c = getchar(); }\n    while (c >= '0' && c <= '9') { x = x * 10 + (c - '0'); c = getchar(); }\n    return x * f;\n}\n\nll readLL() {\n    ll x = 0, f = 1;\n    char c = getchar();\n    while (c < '0' || c > '9') { if (c == '-') f = -1; c = getchar(); }\n    while (c >= '0' && c <= '9') { x = x * 10 + (c - '0'); c = getchar(); }\n    return x * f;\n}\n\nvoid add(int& x, int y) {\n    x += y;\n    if (x >= MOD) x -= MOD;\n}\n\nint main() {\n#ifndef ONLINE_JUDGE\n    freopen(\"matrix.in\", \"r\", stdin);\n    freopen(\"matrix.out\", \"w\", stdout);\n#endif\n    ll m = readLL();\n    n = readInt();\n    E.clear();\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n + 1; ++i) E.a[i][i] = 1;\n    ans = E;\n    \n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n        A[i] = E;\n        for (int j = 1; j <= n + 1; ++j) A[i].a[j][i] = 1;\n    }\n    \n    pre[0] = suf[n + 1] = E;\n    for (; m; m /= n) {\n        ll u = m % n;\n        if (u) {\n            ll s = 0;\n            for (ll v = m / n; v; v /= n) s = (s + v % n) % n;\n            u = (s + u - 1) % n + 1;\n            for (ll cur = u; cur != s; --cur) {\n                if (cur <= 0) cur += n;\n                ans = A[cur] * ans;\n            }\n        }\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) pre[i] = pre[i - 1] * A[i];\n        for (int i = n; i >= 1; --i) suf[i] = A[i] * suf[i + 1];\n        for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) A[i] = suf[i] * pre[i - 1];\n    }\n    \n    int num = 1;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) add(num, ans.a[n + 1][i]);\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", num);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nMOD = 1000000007\nMAXN = 32\n\ndef read_int():\n    x = 0\n    f = 1\n    c = sys.stdin.read(1)\n    while c and (c < '0' or c > '9'):\n        if c == '-':\n            f = -1\n        c = sys.stdin.read(1)\n    while c and '0' <= c <= '9':\n        x = x * 10 + (ord(c) - ord('0'))\n        c = sys.stdin.read(1)\n    return x * f\n\ndef read_ll():\n    x = 0\n    f = 1\n    c = sys.stdin.read(1)\n    while c and (c < '0' or c > '9'):\n        if c == '-':\n            f = -1\n        c = sys.stdin.read(1)\n    while c and '0' <= c <= '9':\n        x = x * 10 + (ord(c) - ord('0'))\n        c = sys.stdin.read(1)\n    return x * f\n\ndef add(x, y):\n    x += y\n    if x >= MOD:\n        x -= MOD\n    return x\n\nclass Matrix:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.a = [[0] * (MAXN) for _ in range(MAXN)]\n    \n    def clear(self):\n        for i in range(MAXN):\n            for j in range(MAXN):\n                self.a[i][j] = 0\n    \n    def output(self):\n        for i in range(1, n + 2):\n            for j in range(1, n + 2):\n                print(self.a[i][j], end='')\n                if j == n + 1:\n                    print()\n                else:\n                    print(' ', end='')\n        print()\n    \n    def __mul__(self, rhs):\n        res = Matrix()\n        for i in range(1, n + 2):\n            for j in range(1, n + 2):\n                for k in range(1, n + 2):\n                    res.a[i][j] = (res.a[i][j] + self.a[i][k] * rhs.a[k][j]) % MOD\n        return res\n\ndef main():\n    global n\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    idx = 0\n    m = int(input_data[idx])\n    idx += 1\n    n = int(input_data[idx])\n    idx += 1\n    \n    E = Matrix()\n    for i in range(1, n + 2):\n        E.a[i][i] = 1\n    \n    ans = Matrix()\n    for i in range(MAXN):\n        for j in range(MAXN):\n            ans.a[i][j] = E.a[i][j]\n    \n    A = [None]  # 1-indexed\n    pre = [None]  # 1-indexed\n    suf = [None]  # 1-indexed\n    \n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        mat = Matrix()\n        for j in range(1, n + 2):\n            mat.a[j][j] = 1\n            mat.a[j][i] = 1\n        A.append(mat)\n    \n    for i in range(n + 2):\n        pre.append(None)\n        suf.append(None)\n    \n    pre[0] = Matrix()\n    for i in range(MAXN):\n        for j in range(MAXN):\n            pre[0].a[i][j] = E.a[i][j]\n    \n    suf[n + 1] = Matrix()\n    for i in range(MAXN):\n        for j in range(MAXN):\n            suf[n + 1].a[i][j] = E.a[i][j]\n    \n    while m > 0:\n        u = m % n\n        m //= n\n        if u != 0:\n            s = 0\n            v = m\n            while v > 0:\n                s = (s + v % n) % n\n                v //= n\n            u = (s + u - 1) % n + 1\n            cur = u\n            while cur != s:\n                if cur <= 0:\n                    cur += n\n                ans = A[cur] * ans\n                cur -= 1\n                if cur <= 0:\n                    cur += n\n        \n        # Update pre array\n        for i in range(1, n + 1):\n            if i == 1:\n                pre[i] = Matrix()\n                for x in range(MAXN):\n                    for y in range(MAXN):\n                        pre[i].a[x][y] = (A[i].a[x][y] if i == 1 else pre[i-1].a[x][y])\n            else:\n                pre[i] = pre[i-1] * A[i]\n        \n        # Update suf array\n        for i in range(n, 0, -1):\n            suf[i] = A[i] * suf[i+1]\n        \n        # Update A array\n        for i in range(1, n + 1):\n            A[i] = suf[i] * pre[i-1]\n    \n    num = 1\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        num = add(num, ans.a[n+1][i])\n    print(num)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.65\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00013600854435935616, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.012601982802152634, -9.417090768693015e-05, -0.038045432418584824, -0.022302992641925812, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0036087408661842346, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -8.344646857949556e-07, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -0.0004885195521637797, -6.198863957251888e-06, -5.960462772236497e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -1.5497195136049413e-06,